# A literal map handed to Object.defineProperties() is not let go at the call: it waits until its entries have been named. One entry here is no accessor as written: it lays a value, and the flow of that
# value to the name on the target is not what keeps the map in sight. So the whole map goes, behind the naming. That is late: the sinks of the scan have been applied by then, and an escape that were only
# noted as a sink would be lost without a word, and Link would prove what does not hold. The edge has to stand in the summary.
